# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, so a clone made on Windows
# rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for most of
# this repo and fatal for the shell scripts: the shebang becomes
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and running one under WSL fails with
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which names a program nobody typed and does not mention line endings at all.
# Forcing LF here means a Windows clone still produces scripts WSL can run.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Unambiguously LF: these are interpreted by a Unix shell wherever they run.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is only ever run by Windows, and CRLF is what a Windows editor
# will produce anyway, so let it keep the local convention.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries. The screenshots are checked in for the README.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
